.SH NAME
.PP
auto-unsupported-os - Display a user-friendly message for unsupported systems

\" Convention:
\" Underline anything that is typed verbatim - commands, etc.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
.nf 
.na
auto-unsupported-os command
.ad
.fi

.SH ARGUMENTS
.nf
.na
command     Name of the calling command, usually $0
.ad
.fi

.SH DESCRIPTION

The
.B auto-unsupported-os
command displays a user-friendly message stating the the
calling script does not support the operating system running it.
This is used by many auto-admin scripts where support for a particular
operating system has not yet been implemented, or where it simply
does not apply.

.SH RETURN VALUES

0 on success, non-zero error codes otherwise.

.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
.na
auto-unsupported-os $0
.ad
.fi

.SH SEE ALSO

auto-admin(8), auto-unsupported-release(8), auto-ostype(8),
auto-os-variant(8)

